{"title":"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is defined for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61fc5f287c1a0e3358fc2842b55a22c184cbef78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x; f(x) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/553679e87340c93fb51f6f1ebbcc48566b91b3e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88aafaaf2cdd8745b28eb77fea3eca215576e9fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)f(b) = f(a + b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Which of the following statements are true?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d99396f9b9df7af48fb5457e20daa4ddc94ad70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I.\\ f(0) = 1 \\qquad \\qquad \\ \\  \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad II.\\ f(-a) = \\frac{1}{f(a)}\\ \\text{for all}\\ a \\\\ III.\\ f(a) = \\sqrt[3]{f(3a)}\\ \\text{for all}\\ a \\qquad IV.\\ f(b) &gt; f(a)\\ \\text{if}\\ b &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"469\" height=\"76\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c0c4135d21671517eaa22a6a3ba9b91c7a7ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{III and IV only} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{I, III, and IV only} \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{I, II, and IV only} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{I, II, and III only} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{All are true.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"509\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbbc0d5c5be8631529615feaec97e34d065387b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I: f(0) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7a58270d4285821716c6093a83541f3ea31dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 0$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. Our equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f11b6b8867934f8a636c59b0994d6a8d42c2c1bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)f(0) = f(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf24e88058a6fdef1dddad3aa7562a7cf7109b32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is always true.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/2/fd2519da7e50d4cc8a2e854f85f2d295e48f7b3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II: f(-a) = \\frac{1}{f(a)} \\text{ for all } a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"211\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a204298d50e2587a7218586c22d1a9cc617d637d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = -a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />. Our equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0c3e9c9110f3b55efbe4854099af333b6935160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)f(-a) = f(0) = 1 \\longrightarrow f(-a) = \\frac{1}{f(a)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"328\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is always true.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f01437931a791a77db03ba236d76567a7c46e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$III: f(a) = \\sqrt[3] {f(3a)} \\text{ for all } a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"230\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>First let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/2510c0ee8fa65393d9a6689e806595cd57234ea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = a$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c833b4a106e2a49293ea85f6f39b2bec3ada813d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)f(a) = f(2a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />. Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff8001670b48cdd67d910642bc830258fc70e863.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2a$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f188abb95cab5deabec45aab651974703b4587e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3a) = f(a)f(2a) = f(a)^3 \\longrightarrow f(a) = \\sqrt[3] {f(3a)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"375\" height=\"35\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40a16dd7d1d1fedb353096f50c74ce0da7d1d093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$III$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is always true.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d44f7f92f38ac3b39a8e799c4e6fbf34f1597fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IV: f(b) &gt; f(a) \\text{ if } b &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"20\" />\nThis is false. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f89e8205d4cc476f36512b2c0cee23c1915cd24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 2^{-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"21\" />, for example. It satisfies the conditions but makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77937bd511ef606638c7ac4dc32e42f09545d8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> false. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77937bd511ef606638c7ac4dc32e42f09545d8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> is not always true.\n</p><p><br />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb5e40d1aea8a597221dac4468676eceecb40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I, II, \\text{ and } III$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> are true, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>- mako17\n</p><p>Note: For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77937bd511ef606638c7ac4dc32e42f09545d8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />, one may also disprove it with simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39d2a273ecd239f0cc9334d3134539a0174b4df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME\" title=\"1975 AHSME\">1975 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1975 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1975\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"19